      "facts": [
        "much ACTIVE time a grant may spend once its run has started.",
        "The most one gap between two reserved calls can add to a grant's active time. A longer gap is the run waiting (on the user, or on a long command Desktop is timing itself), and counts only this much.",
        "A grant's active time after one more reserved call at `nowMs`: the previous total plus the gap since the last call, capped at {@link SPONSORED_ACTIVE_GAP_CAP_MS}. The first call (`lastCallAtMs` null) adds nothing, and a clock that went backwards adds nothing.",
        "Whether a grant has spent its active window.",
        "Wall clock: the server no longer applies it (it meters active time), so it only bounds a client that cannot pause its clock while waiting on the user.",
        "Called with two arguments (the legacy Convex sweep), it is the second arm from `runningAtMs`."
      ],
