        "calls": 1,
        "text": "The time limit for a sponsored task now counts only the minutes the assistant is actively working, instead of stopping the clock at one hour of real-world time. This change primarily affects advertisers who fund these tasks and the desktop users who run them. As a result, a sponsored task no longer dies after sixty minutes if it is paused while you answer a prompt or wait for a step to finish, because pauses no longer drain the budget.",
